class.description:
Adapter is the port of [i]RecyclerView.Adapter[/i]. A GDScript subclass must implement
[method _get_item_count], [method _create_item] and [method _bind_item]; it may optionally
override [method _get_item_view_type], [method _get_item_extent] and [method _get_item_id].

[b]Minimal subclass[/b]:
[codeblock]
class MyAdapter extends Adapter:
    var items: Array = []

    func _get_item_count() -> int:
        return items.size()

    func _create_item(parent: Control, view_type: int) -> ViewHolder:
        var vh := ViewHolder.new()
        var label := Label.new()
        label.set_size(Vector2(200, 40))
        vh.set_control(label)
        return vh

    func _bind_item(holder: ViewHolder, position: int) -> void:
        (holder.get_control() as Label).text = str(items[position])
[/codeblock]

The engine calls [method create_view_holder] (which invokes [method _create_item]) when a new
position needs a holder, then [method bind_view_holder] (which invokes [method _bind_item]).
Data changes are reported through the [code]notify_item_*[/code] methods; when the adapter is
attached to a RecyclerView the notifications are forwarded to it automatically.
